<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS4" title="In 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.4 </span>Framework versus CoT and Direct Prompting</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS4.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.4 Framework versus CoT and Direct Prompting ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Compartmentalisation improves accuracy by 30+ points over CoT and Direct prompting</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS4.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4.4 Framework versus CoT and Direct Prompting ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Even misclassified solver prompts outperform CoT and Direct baselines</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS4.SSS0.Px3" title="In 4.4 Framework versus CoT and Direct Prompting ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Oracle Planner confirms solvers can follow schemas when routed correctly</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS5" title="In 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.5 </span>Verifier Performance</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.5 Verifier Performance ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Verifier judgments frequently exceed solver accuracy across families</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS5.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4.5 Verifier Performance ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Verification is easier in causal and risk reasoning, harder in composition</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS6" title="In 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.6 </span>Effects of Refinement</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.6 Effects of Refinement ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Refinement corrects up to 39% of epistemic errors through factual edits</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS6.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4.6 Effects of Refinement ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Refinement is rare but highly accurate in causal reasoning, common but ineffective in composition</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS6.SSS0.Px3" title="In 4.6 Effects of Refinement ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Fact errors are easier to fix than reasoning errors, limiting compositional gains</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S4.SS7" title="In 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">4.7 </span>Qualitative Analysis of Representative Items</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS7.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.7 Qualitative Analysis of Representative Items ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Causal Attribution (Problem 6).</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS7.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4.7 Qualitative Analysis of Representative Items ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Compositional Grounding (Problem 12).</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS7.SSS0.Px3" title="In 4.7 Qualitative Analysis of Representative Items ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Epistemic Verification (Problem 16).</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS7.SSS0.Px4" title="In 4.7 Qualitative Analysis of Representative Items ‣ 4 Results ‣ Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Risk State Abstraction (Problem 39).</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S5" title="In Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5 </span>Future Work</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S6" title="In Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">6 </span>Related Work</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S7" title="In Compartmentalised Agentic Reasoning for Clinical NLI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">7 </span>Conclusion</span></a></li>
